All files above are in app/Sources/BridgeplayApp/Resources/. The engine's ntdll
is patched at setup with detours built from ntdll-patch/ (detour*.bin in the
same folder). nvapi64-shim.dll is Bridgeplay's own code, built from nvapi-shim/.

Shipped in the one-click installer (Bridgeplay-Installer.zip)
-------------------------------------------------------------

The installer carries no app (Install.command downloads Bridgeplay.zip from this
project's GitHub releases). It carries these unmodified archives, so a Mac can set
up without downloading them. The app installs the same archives (pinned by sha256
in app/Sources/BridgeplayApp/Model/FreeEngine.swift) when they are not there.

  DXMT (dxmt-e94c312.tar.gz, built from https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt at
      e94c312f5c054263acf261cfa109edf13e757587; docs/DXMT.md), Copyright (c)
      2023-2026 Feifan He for CodeWeavers, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
  DXVK-macOS 1.10.3 (dxvk-macOS-async-v1.10.3-20230507-repack-builtin.tar.gz from
      https://github.com/Gcenx/DXVK-macOS/releases/tag/v1.10.3-20230507-repack),
      zlib license.
  Apple Game Porting Toolkit redistributables (gptk/: external/ with
      D3DMetal.framework and libd3dshared.dylib, and wine/, from the toolkit's
      /redist/lib directory), Apple software under Apple's license, shipped as
      GPTK-License.rtf. Apple's license allows distributing it "solely for
      non-commercial purposes" (section 2A(iii)), and allows the Framework and
      Redistributables to be "distributed separately from the Apple Software"
      (section 2C). The wine/ folder is not Wine: wine/x86_64-windows holds only
      Apple's proprietary D3DMetal front-end DLLs (d3d10, d3d11, d3d12,
      d3d12core, dxgi, nvapi64 and nvngx-on-metalfx.dll), and wine/x86_64-unix
      holds only symlinks to external/libd3dshared.dylib. Apple publishes no
      source for them, and none is offered here. How each condition of Apple's license is met:
      docs/GPTK-LICENSE.md.

The license texts of DXMT and DXVK ship next to these archives in the installer.

Not shipped in the installer: the WineCX runtime (Libraries.tar.gz from
https://github.com/dappermint/winecx-gptk, pinned in
app/Sources/BridgeplayApp/Model/FreeEngineWinecx.swift). Besides Wine it bundles
third-party libraries, some under the GNU GPL (FFmpeg built with --enable-gpl
--enable-version3, x264, x265, libdvdcss, libdvdread, libdvdnav), whose
corresponding source neither dappermint/winecx-gptk nor Bridgeplay publishes. So
Bridgeplay does not redistribute that archive: the app downloads it straight from
dappermint/winecx-gptk's GitHub release on the user's Mac. Installers up to
Bridgeplay 0.7.50 carried it, which is why it was taken out;
those old installer downloads have been removed from the releases.

